  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What it works out",
      "items": [
        "2*nx + 1 sigma points, spread about x by the square root of P",
        "Y[i] = f(X[i], u), each point through the TRUE function",
        "x = sum of w[i]*Y[i], and P from how far the Y[i] landed apart"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "How it differs from ekf",
      "items": [
        "The extended filter asks what the model does to a straight line",
        "This asks what the model does to a handful of real points",
        "No derivative is taken anywhere at all"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "What can break it",
      "items": [
        "The square root of P is what spreads the points, thus it must exist",
        "P must stay positive definite, and rounding can break that",
        "It is the one thing that fails here where the extended filter would not"
      ]
